# Copy to ignored user.bazelrc. Keep credentials outside this file and Git.
# See docs/build-observability.md. Remote upload is currently disabled.

# Shared downloads/action caches may live on another volume. Do not share one
# output_base between worktrees; use a private output_user_root if relocation is
# needed, so Bazel derives a distinct output base from each workspace path.
# startup --output_user_root=/path/to/private/bazel-output
# common --repository_cache=/path/to/shared/bazel-repo
# build --disk_cache=/path/to/shared/bazel-disk

# Apply machine budgets deliberately; memory is in MB and is a scheduling budget,
# not a limit on each process. Worker limits apply per worker key.
# build --jobs=2
# build --local_resources=cpu=2
# build --local_resources=memory=4096
# build --jvmopt=-Xmx768m
# build --host_jvmopt=-Xmx1536m

# --config=local updates MODULE.bazel.lock; --config=ci rejects lockfile drift.
# --config=debug prints action commands and retains sandbox files.
# BEP/profile destinations must be unique per invocation, supplied on the command
# line together with the invocation UUID and build metadata (see the guide).

# BES remains disabled by owner choice. The bes profile sets bounded synchronous
# transport behavior only. Do not add a destination or authentication until a
# specific private endpoint and credential helper have been verified and remote
# upload has been explicitly enabled. Never paste a token into --remote_header.
